From 46966b4fae706a3b0bbad178366e231a144e6b2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Maxime=20M=C3=A9r=C3=A9?= <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 11:43:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 563/572] fix(stm32mp2): ignore intentional USB reset assert
 return value in BL2
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The USB subsystem reset performed before the UART programmer is used
intentionally ignores the return value of stm32mp_reset_assert(). If the
function returns a timeout, the reset has already been performed, and the
error is not important enough to justify a panic.

Cast the return value to void to make this intent explicit.

Coverity issue: CID 1209910: Unchecked return value in bl2_el3_plat_arch_setup

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 8dc22d210ba67429a326e01ec4f3925f1e824b8b fix(stm32mp2): ignore intentional USB reset assert return value in BL2]
Change-Id: Id860a4835c22540d9d9d9144efee0b0a5069930d
Signed-off-by: Maxime Méré <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/597394
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
---
 plat/st/stm32mp2/bl2_plat_setup.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/st/stm32mp2/bl2_plat_setup.c b/plat/st/stm32mp2/bl2_plat_setup.c
index 8b7e13886b..6bd656dd5d 100644
--- a/plat/st/stm32mp2/bl2_plat_setup.c
+++ b/plat/st/stm32mp2/bl2_plat_setup.c
@@ -503,11 +503,11 @@ void bl2_el3_plat_arch_setup(void)
 #if STM32MP_UART_PROGRAMMER
 	/* Reset USB sub-system to avoid all spurious transactions */
 #if STM32MP21
-	stm32mp_reset_assert(OTG_R, TIMEOUT_US_1MS);
+	(void)stm32mp_reset_assert(OTG_R, TIMEOUT_US_1MS);
 #else /* !STM32MP21 */
-	stm32mp_reset_assert(USB3DR_R, TIMEOUT_US_1MS);
+	(void)stm32mp_reset_assert(USB3DR_R, TIMEOUT_US_1MS);
 #endif /* STM32MP21 */
-	stm32mp_reset_assert(USB2PHY2_R, TIMEOUT_US_1MS);
+	(void)stm32mp_reset_assert(USB2PHY2_R, TIMEOUT_US_1MS);
 #endif /* STM32MP_UART_PROGRAMMER */
 
 #if STM32MP_DDR_FIP_IO_STORAGE || TRUSTED_BOARD_BOOT
-- 
